bench/corpus/external-v1.yml .. external-v4.yml and bench/corpus/direction-v1.yml
(generated by tools/corpus/build_external.py and tools/corpus/build_direction.py), and the sentences
derived from them in experiments/tier2/corpus/ and experiments/paraphrase/
  Requirement sentences taken from other projects, pinned by commit, then transformed:
  - StrictDoc, https://github.com/strictdoc-project/strictdoc
    Apache-2.0, Copyright 2020-2026 Stanislav Pankevich, Maryna Balioura.
  - Doorstop, https://github.com/doorstop-dev/doorstop
    LGPL-3.0, Doorstop contributors. The sentences are Doorstop's own requirements text.
    The LGPL-3.0 text (LICENSES/LGPL-3.0.txt) and the GPL-3.0 it supplements
    (LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt) are shipped with this repository. req does not link Doorstop.
  - PROMISE NFR, Jane Cleland-Huang, Sepideh Mazrouee, Huang Liguo, Dan Port,
    https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.268542 , CC-BY-4.0 (the Zenodo record's stated licence).
    The generator reads a 969-row expanded copy of the data set from
    https://github.com/mahdikabootari/Software-Requirements-Classification (no licence file).
    The licence of the rows added to the original data set was NOT verified. If you hold rights
    in them and object to their use, open an issue and they will be removed.

